      "width": 298.282,
      "height": 21.25,
      "text": "StrictMode mounts everything twice",
      "originalText": "StrictMode mounts everything twice",
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 373210913,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 134139404,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1735689600000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "index": "am",
      "id": "lifecycle-text-43",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 14,
      "y": 804,
      "width": 861.4375000000001,
      "height": 46.875,
      "text": "In development React mounts, unmounts and mounts again without re-rendering: create, dispose, create. That is why the mount is built by\nthe effect that destroys it. A mount built in useMemo is not re-evaluated on the second setup, so the second setup ran against the object\nthe first cleanup had already disposed — a CancelledError in development, while production worked.",
      "originalText": "In development React mounts, unmounts and mounts again without re-rendering: create, dispose, create. That is why the mount is built by\nthe effect that destroys it. A mount built in useMemo is not re-evaluated on the second setup, so the second setup ran against the object\nthe first cleanup had already disposed — a CancelledError in development, while production worked.",
      "fontSize": 12.5,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
